    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0951" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg827"/>

                <head>No. 497.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Señor de
                        Zamacona.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-04-19"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 19,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 13th instant, in further relation to the outrages committed
                    by outlaws along the frontier districts in Mexico from the Territory of Arizona,
                    and suggesting in the interest of peace and prosperity between the governments
                    of the United States and Mexico that measures be speedily taken for the
                    suppression of the depredators.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, I have the pleasure to inform you that a copy of your note has been
                    communicated to the Secretary of the Interior, for his information and such
                    future action as he and the authorities of the Territory of Arizona may be able
                    to pursue to the desired end.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
